    "['ip sla schedule [parameter1] start-time [parameter2]', [{'para_map': [], 'trans_command': 'set services rpm probe test1 test test1 start now', 'parent_command': [], 'root': 'set services rpm probe test1 test test1 start now', 'source': 'llm', 'origin_reponse': 'Here\\'s the Juniper equivalent of the Cisco `ip sla schedule 1 start-time now` command:\\n\\n##\\nset services rpm probe test1 test test1 start now\\n##\\n\\nExplanation:\\n- `services rpm` is Juniper\\'s equivalent of Cisco\\'s IP SLA (now called RPM - Real-Time Performance Monitoring)\\n- `probe test1` creates a probe with ID \"test1\" (equivalent to Cisco\\'s SLA 1)\\n- `test test1` creates a test under that probe\\n- `start now` mirrors the \"start-time now\" functionality from Cisco\\n\\nNote: Juniper\\'s RPM configuration requires additional context (like probe type, target, etc.) which would be set by other commands equivalent to the Cisco IP SLA configuration.', 'trans_template': 'set services rpm probe test1 test test1 start now'}]]": 1,
